# Xcode Generated Files and Directories

## Build Products
# These are the compiled binaries and intermediate build files.
build/
DerivedData/
*.xcarchive/
*.xcactivitylog
*.dSYM
*.dSYM.zip
*.ipa # Universal application archive

## User/Workspace Specific Files
# These contain user-specific settings, breakpoints, window layouts, etc.
# They should not be shared across developers.
xcuserdata/
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
!*.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/ # Keep the project's workspace file
!*.xcworkspace/ # Keep the general workspace file (if not part of a project)
*.xcodeproj/*.mode1v3
*.xcodeproj/*.mode2v3
*.xcodeproj/*.pbxuser
*.xcodeproj/*.perspectivev3
*.xcodeproj/*~.nib
*.xcscmblueprint
*.xccheckout
*.xcprofile
*.xcodesamplecode
*.xctestrun

## Swift Package Manager (SPM)
# Files generated by SPM for dependencies.
.swiftpm/
# The Packages directory itself is typically ignored
# Packages/

## CocoaPods
# The official recommendation is often to *commit* the Pods/ directory for consistent builds.
# However, if your team prefers not to commit, uncomment the line below.
Pods/

## Carthage
# Compiled frameworks and their source code.
Carthage/Build/
Carthage/Checkouts/

## Fastlane (Automation Tool)
# Generated reports, screenshots, and temporary files from Fastlane.
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
fastlane/screenshots/**/*.png # Adjust path if screenshots are elsewhere
fastlane/test_output

## Code Injection Tools (e.g., InjectionIII)
.injection/

## Playground Files
*.playground/timeline
*.playground/Sources/
*.playground/Resources/

## Generated Documentation
# If you use tools like Jazzy to generate documentation.
docs/

## CoreML Generated Models
# Compiled CoreML models (if you're not committing the models directly).
*.mlmodelc/

## Storyboard/XIB Intermediate Files
*.storyboardc/
*.xib/
*.nib/

## Asset Catalog Intermediate Files
Assets.car

## Precompiled Headers (PCH) and Module Maps Cache
*.pch.pth
*.hmap
ModuleCache/

## Other Caches and Logs
*.log
*.temp
*.tmp
*.db # Database files (e.g., SQLite dbs created during development)

## Crash Reports
*.crash

# General C/C++/Objective-C Build Artifacts (not always Xcode-specific)

## Object Files
*.o
*.obj
*.lo
*.slo
*.ko

## Compiled Libraries (Dynamic/Static)
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.a
*.lib
*.lai

## Executables
*.exe
a.out
*.out # Generic compiler output executable

## Precompiled Headers
*.gch
*.pch

## Linker Output
*.ilk
*.map
*.exp

## Debugging / Core Dumps
*.d
*.core

## Compiler / Build System Specific (e.g., CMake, Make)
# CMake
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
install_manifest.txt
CPackConfig.cmake
_CPack_Packages/

# Makefiles (if generated, not source)
Makefile.local

# Dependency files
.deps/

# Other temporary files
*~ # Backup files created by text editors
*.bak
*.swp # Vim swap files
*.swo # Vim swap files
*.swn # Vim swap files

# Operating System Files (macOS specific)
.DS_Store
.localized
.Trashes
._* # Resource forks
.Spotlight-V100 # Spotlight index
.TemporaryItems
.fseventsd # File system events log
